# The programs this system knows how to fetch.
#
#   name | kind | file | address | one line about it
#
# `kind` is `native` for a program built for this system and `windows` for one
# built for Windows, which runs under the translation layer.
#
# Two things decide whether an entry will work, and both are checked before
# anything is kept on the disk:
#
#   - it has to be one file. A program that arrives as an installer, an
#     archive, or a set of pieces has nothing here to unpack it.
#   - a Windows program has to be built for x86-64. A 32-bit one is a
#     different instruction set, not an older version of the same thing, and
#     this system will say so rather than install it.
#
# Anything not listed here can still be fetched by giving its address
# directly, which is the general case; this list is only the short cut.

7-Zip | windows | 7zr.exe | https://www.7-zip.org/a/7zr.exe | A standalone archive extractor. Published as a 32-bit program, so it downloads and is then refused - which is what that refusal looks like.
